I have a problem with AnyRepr...

```
        template<typename A, typename B>
        TestEqual(const A &a, const B &b)
                : TestEqual(
                        std::make_shared<const AnyRepr<A>>(a),
                        std::make_shared<const AnyRepr<B>>(b)
                )
        {
        }

        TestEqual(const std::shared_ptr<const StringRepr> &a, const std::shared_ptr<const StringRepr> &b);
```

Always select first ctor and recursive templates... Why?

Have an idea.

```
TstTemplate(
      make_shared<StringRep>(
            make_shared<Object>
     ),
     IsContainText("hello")
);
```
StringRepr can adopt any object to String.
